# forward_xyb magetypes consolidation bench (W43-2 chunk-6)
timestamp: 2026-05-18T20:55:00Z
hostname: lilith (Ryzen 9 7950X, 128 GB RAM, water-cooled)
git_commit: pending-commit
phase_baseline_at:  3915dd4c (main: W43-2 chunk-5 pixel_loss consolidation, xyb.rs pre-consolidation)
phase_post_at:      this commit (W43-2 chunk-6 magetypes-consolidated forward_xyb + inverse_xyb_planar)
sizes: [256, 512, 1024, 2048, 4096]
samples_per_cell: 15
warmup: 3
purpose: validates that the magetypes(define(f32x8), v4, v3, neon, wasm128, scalar)
         consolidation in jxl-encoder-simd/src/xyb.rs (forward_xyb_impl and
         inverse_xyb_planar_impl) preserves wall-clock vs the prior 3-variant
         hand-written code (AVX2 / NEON / WASM128) and the scalar fallback.
kernel:   forward_xyb — linear RGB → XYB (matrix mul + clamp + Newton-Raphson cbrt in f64 + mix)
shape:    one call per encode over the full width × height f32 plane (SoA: 3 in, 3 out).
input:    3 synthetic planes (R, G, B), each filled with low-freq sinusoids in [0, 1].
load_note: bench was run with system load (other agents' work consuming several cores);
           use best_ms columns as the least noise-sensitive signal. See
           ~/.claude/projects/-home-lilith-work-zen-jxl-encoder/memory/jj_concurrent_workspace_failure_mode_2026-05-18.md
           for noise-handling discipline.
