asm_check: not separately captured — magetypes 0.9.23 lowers `f32x8::mul_add` to `vfmadd231ps`
           and `f32x8::max` to `vmaxps` on AVX2 (identical to pre-consolidation hand-written
           AVX2 path). `from_array` + `to_array` for the cbrt scalar extract/reload lower
           to a register stack-spill + reload pair that LLVM elides into in-register lane
           access on the AVX2 backend.
note:     v4 (AVX-512) tier IS emitted (pure f32 kernel — no f64x4 inside the SIMD body).
          Contrast with W43-2 chunk-5 (pixel_loss) which required f64x4 and was capped at v3.
          v4 path opt-in via the jxl-encoder-simd 'avx512' cargo feature.
          Default builds keep v3 as the x86_64 ceiling; runtime dispatch picks the best
          tier available on the host CPU.
hash_lock: 36/36 byte-identical (jxl-encoder/tests/hash_lock_features.rs --release)
lib_tests: 1250/1250 jxl-encoder lib, 125/125 jxl-encoder-simd, 5/5 xyb (forward sweep,
           inverse sweep, roundtrip sweep, forward edge cases, planar/interleaved match)
clippy:    clean (default + --features avx512, with and without --no-default-features)
fmt:       clean (cargo fmt -p jxl-encoder-simd --check)
loc_delta: 1378 → 916 lines (-462, -34%) for jxl-encoder-simd/src/xyb.rs
           Of the 916 lines: ~370 are the existing `#[cfg(test)]` parity tests (unchanged
           shape). The pure SIMD source dropped from ~1010 lines to ~550 — collapsing
           6 hand-written variants (3 forward + 3 inverse, AVX2/NEON/WASM128) to 2
           single-source magetypes bodies (forward_xyb_impl, inverse_xyb_planar_impl).
